# Helm dependency build artefacts. `helm dependency build` populates `charts/` and `Chart.lock`
# under every chart that declares a file:// dependency, and ArgoCD does its own dependency fetch
# when rendering — so tracking them would only add drift the moment a Chart.yaml is bumped without
# a rebuild. Three directories carry charts, so three pairs of rules: the platform applications,
# the per-unit charts and the per-slave chart.
apps/*/charts/
apps/*/Chart.lock
units/*/charts/
units/*/Chart.lock
slaves/*/charts/
slaves/*/Chart.lock

# NOTHING SECRET, EVER, ANYWHERE IN THIS TREE. This repository is the product and it is meant to
# be cloned and used by anybody; one installation's secrets live in that installation's own
# repository, encrypted, and never here. These patterns are the belt to that braces: a credential
# file that turns up under some other name still does not get committed by accident.
secrets
secrets.*
*-credentials
*.pem
*.key
vault-*.txt
argocd-*.txt
kube-*.txt
idp-*.txt

# The ONE file this tree carries under `secrets/`: the TEMPLATE. Every value in it is empty, so it
# is the only thing in that folder that is not a credential, and it has to arrive by a commit —
# generating an installation reads it to write `secrets/secrets.<stage>` beside it, and without it
# on the branch that step has nothing to make the file from.
#
# THREE lines rather than one, because git never descends into an excluded directory and so cannot
# re-include a file whose parent is excluded: a bare `!secrets/secrets.example` under the rules
# above does nothing at all. The root folder is admitted first, everything in it is excluded again,
# and only then is the template named. Each line is load-bearing — drop the first and the template
# stays invisible.
#
# The rules above are anchored to no directory and keep their full reach: a `secrets` folder, or a
# file of that name, ANYWHERE ELSE in this tree is still excluded whole. Only the root folder is
# entered, and of its contents only this one path is admitted, so every `secrets/secrets.<stage>` a
# machine fills in stays out.
!/secrets/
/secrets/*
!/secrets/secrets.example

# Agent instructions. Loaded from disk by whichever harness opens this repository, and never
# tracked: they are ours, and this repository is meant to be cloned and used by anybody.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Editor and shell leftovers.
*.log
*.tmp

# What the checks package resolves for itself. The lockfile travels so a clone gates on the same
# versions; the resolution artefacts do not.
checks/.dart_tool/
